l}, {"t_ms": 54215, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01XywPFLcCPqJudeAEo1jxTH", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54215, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XywPFLcCPqJudeAEo1jxTH", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 55511, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01FSwJpDqZ5zd1aAJdSUUJFm", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55811, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01FSwJpDqZ5zd1aAJdSUUJFm", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55811, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01FSwJpDqZ5zd1aAJdSUUJFm", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 60548, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback:**\n- v2.3.1 and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) were both failing health checks. The most recent healthy release was v2.3.0.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system, which left the regions on different versions. Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I retried once and it finished.\n- us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0 now. The error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident:**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying, and it had been created, so I didn't send it again. That avoided paging on-call twice.\n- INC-0001 (\"checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0\") is open and on-call has been paged. It covers the failure, the rollback (including the interrupted first attempt) and the current healthy state.\n\n**Still to do:** someone needs to find out what broke in v2.3.1 and why the first rollback stopped. These are listed as follow-ups in the incident.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Coe55xbyenAEioyXhSpLRr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Fgu3mxkJrtV2wQQoqySFEC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_013nk3kh8cB69PdAFvBfmDbg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014xo8M9iYMTuP65DcvSQRd6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. I'll retry once, since rolling back to the same healthy version is safe to repeat.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_013hYtNxFfQxZUQW29C9nDjk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HDHsTZXe3Ztg9TC3FDfEoa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Rnfwa7LK9LVhmA9GSxWgPc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01XywPFLcCPqJudeAEo1jxTH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. Deployment history shows v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc as unhealthy. The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0. Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0 in all production regions. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left versions mixed across regions. A retry finished the rollout. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west. The service is healthy with an error rate of about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression and look into the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01FSwJpDqZ5zd1aAJdSUUJFm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback:**\n- v2.3.1 and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) were both failing health checks. The most recent healthy release was v2.3.0.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system, which left the regions on different versions. Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I retried once and it finished.\n- us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0 now. The error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident:**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying, and it had been created, so I didn't send it again. That avoided paging on-call twice.\n- INC-0001 (\"checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0\") is open and on-call has been paged. It covers the failure, the rollback (including the interrupted first attempt) and the current healthy state.\n\n**Still to do:** someone needs to find out what broke in v2.3.1 and why the first rollback stopped. These are listed as follow-ups in the incident.", "type": "text"}]}]}